# Truth Serum — The Daily Bugle

**Problem:** "The Daily Bugle Truth Serum" — fake text detection.
New York's been flooded with AI-generated news, fake interviews, and
fabricated posts. This gives readers a "Spider-Sense" for whether a
piece of text was written by a person or a machine.

**Live demo (no setup):** the original prototype runs inside Claude's
artifact environment at
https://claude.ai/artifact/7zV5yDRnwfYAWViSWMULTD — it needs no API
key because Claude supplies the model call for free. The version in
this repo is a standalone rebuild you can host anywhere (GitHub
Pages, Netlify, your own server), which is why it needs a key of its
own.

## How it works

1. The user pastes text into the "Exhibit A" box.
2. `js/app.js` sends the text to the Anthropic Messages API
   (`POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages`) with a prompt that
   asks Claude to act as a skeptical editor and return strict JSON:
   a verdict (`human` / `ai` / `uncertain`), a 0–100 confidence
   score, a one-line "tell," and 3–4 concrete case notes (sentence
   rhythm, hedging, generic transitions, etc.).
3. The UI renders that JSON as a stamped verdict, a confidence
   meter, and a typewritten notes list.

No backend, no database — it's a static site that talks straight to
the Anthropic API from the browser.

