## Setup

1. Get an API key from https://console.anthropic.com/
2. Open `index.html` (locally, or after deploying — see below).
3. Paste your key into the "Desk credentials" box and click **Save
   key**. It's stored in `localStorage`, scoped to whatever domain
   is hosting the page, and only ever sent to `api.anthropic.com`.
4. Paste text and click **Run the Analysis**.

### ⚠️ About the API key

This demo calls the Anthropic API **directly from the browser**,
which means the key lives in the visitor's own browser storage, not
in your code — so don't hardcode a key into `app.js` or commit one to
GitHub. For a real product (not a hackathon demo), move the API call
behind a small serverless function (Cloudflare Worker, Vercel
function, etc.) so the key never reaches the client at all.

## Deploying to GitHub Pages

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Truth Serum — AI text detector"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<you>/truth-serum.git
git push -u origin main
```

Then in the repo: **Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → main
→ / (root)**. Your site will be live at
`https://<you>.github.io/truth-serum/`.

## Customizing

- **Model:** change `MODEL` at the top of `js/app.js` if
  `claude-sonnet-5` isn't current by the time you use this — check
  https://docs.claude.com for the latest model names.
- **Theme:** all colors are CSS custom properties in `:root` at the
  top of `css/style.css` (dark mode included via
  `prefers-color-scheme`).
- **Prompt:** `buildPrompt()` in `app.js` is where the detection
  logic actually lives — tune it to weight different signals.

## Known limitations (worth saying out loud to judges)

- This is an LLM's *opinion*, not a forensic tool — no detector
  (this one included) is reliably accurate, and heavily-edited human
  writing or very short snippets can fool it either direction.
- Client-side API keys aren't safe for a public production app —
  see the warning above.
